Relevant columns and how they will be used  

`midyear_population.year` : filter to the reference year 2017  
`midyear_population.country_code` / `country_name` : join key and readable country name  
`midyear_population.midyear_population` : total population denominator  

`midyear_population_5yr_age_sex.year` : filter to 2017  
`midyear_population_5yr_age_sex.country_code` : join key  
`midyear_population_5yr_age_sex.total_flag` : take “A” (individual 5‑year age groups) for the numerator, or “*” (all ages) when we need a control check  
`midyear_population_5yr_age_sex.starting_age` / `ending_age` : select the five 0‑4, 5‑9, 10‑14, 15‑19, 20‑24 groups → population <25  
`midyear_population_5yr_age_sex.midyear_population` : population figure to be summed for numerator  

Typical conditions that will be used  
• `WHERE year = 2017`  
• `WHERE total_flag = 'A'`  
• `WHERE starting_age < 25`  (or `ending_age <= 24`)  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑solution BigQuery SQL snippets (each returns ≤20 rows) that can be run in sequence to arrive at the answer. Replace nothing – all identifiers are fully‑qualified.  

```sql
-- 1) Distinct years available in the “5‑year age group” table
SELECT DISTINCT year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Sample of 5‑year age‑group populations in 2017
SELECT country_name, starting_age, ending_age, midyear_population
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
WHERE year = 2017
  AND total_flag = 'A'
  AND starting_age < 25
ORDER BY country_name, starting_age
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) What five‑year buckets actually exist in 2017?
SELECT DISTINCT starting_age, ending_age, age_group_indicator
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
WHERE year = 2017
  AND total_flag = 'A'
ORDER BY starting_age
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Raw total population in 2017 for a quick check
SELECT country_name, midyear_population
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population`
WHERE year = 2017
ORDER BY midyear_population DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Sum of population under 25 for each country (no % yet)
SELECT country_code,
       country_name,
       SUM(midyear_population) AS pop_under_25
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
WHERE year = 2017
  AND total_flag = 'A'
  AND starting_age < 25
GROUP BY country_code, country_name
ORDER BY pop_under_25 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Join with total population to compute the % under 25
SELECT u.country_name,
       u.pop_under_25,
       t.midyear_population AS total_pop,
       100 * u.pop_under_25 / t.midyear_population AS pct_under_25
FROM (
      SELECT country_code,
             country_name,
             SUM(midyear_population) AS pop_under_25
      FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
      WHERE year = 2017
        AND total_flag = 'A'
        AND starting_age < 25
      GROUP BY country_code, country_name
     ) AS u
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population` AS t
  ON u.country_code = t.country_code
 AND t.year = 2017
ORDER BY pct_under_25 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Same as (6) but restrict to the very top country
SELECT u.country_name,
       100 * u.pop_under_25 / t.midyear_population AS pct_under_25
FROM (
      SELECT country_code,
             SUM(midyear_population) AS pop_under_25
      FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
      WHERE year = 2017
        AND total_flag = 'A'
        AND starting_age < 25
      GROUP BY country_code
     ) AS u
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population` AS t
  ON u.country_code = t.country_code
 AND t.year = 2017
ORDER BY pct_under_25 DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 8) Quick verification: ratio of “*” (all ages) rows to total pop table
SELECT g.country_name,
       g.midyear_population AS star_table_total,
       t.midyear_population AS plain_total
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex` AS g
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population`        AS t
  ON g.country_code = t.country_code
 AND g.year = t.year
WHERE g.year = 2017
  AND g.total_flag = '*'
ORDER BY ABS(g.midyear_population - t.midyear_population) DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Countries that might be missing any of the five needed age buckets
SELECT country_name,
       COUNTIF(starting_age < 25) AS buckets_under_25_present
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
WHERE year = 2017
  AND total_flag = 'A'
GROUP BY country_name
HAVING buckets_under_25_present < 5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL QUERY – country with the highest % of population under 25 in 2017
SELECT p.country_name,
       SUM(g.midyear_population)                     AS population_under_25,
       p.midyear_population                          AS total_population,
       100 * SUM(g.midyear_population) / p.midyear_population AS pct_under_25
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population`        AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex` AS g
  ON p.country_code = g.country_code
 AND p.year        = g.year
WHERE p.year = 2017
  AND g.total_flag = 'A'          -- individual five‑year groups
  AND g.starting_age < 25         -- ages 0‑24
GROUP BY p.country_name, p.midyear_population
ORDER BY pct_under_25 DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

