Successfully corrected. SQL:
--Description / Thinking process:
-- Objective: confirm whether any country lacks one of the five 5‑year age buckets (0‑4 … 20‑24) in 2017.
-- Approach:
--   1. Use the 5‑year‑age table for 2017 with total_flag='A'.
--   2. For each country_code, COUNT all rows whose starting_age < 25.
--   3. Display the counts (expecting 5 when data are complete) ordered ascending,
--      so any country with fewer than five buckets will surface at the top.

SELECT
  country_code,
  ANY_VALUE(country_name) AS country_name,
  COUNTIF(starting_age < 25) AS buckets_under_25_present
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
WHERE year = 2017
  AND total_flag = 'A'
GROUP BY country_code
ORDER BY buckets_under_25_present ASC, country_name
LIMIT 20;
